    </header>
    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="9" relname="span">Intuitiveness should be clearly included as a requirement specification in software engineering.</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="13" relname="preparation">Lets take an example of using an online banking application.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="13" relname="span">Humans to need substantial intelligent computer support in dealing with the technical aspects of the banking site,</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="3" relname="elaboration">for example, security, encryption, password protection, etc.</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="15" relname="span">A majority of the users are not and will never become information technology specialists.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="7" relname="antithesis">They do need computers that are not only tools,</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="14" relname="span">but assistants to the user.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="14" relname="elaboration">Users and their computer assistants have to talk in an intuitive way to each other.</segment>
        <group id="9" type="span"/>
        <group id="10" type="span" parent="1" relname="evidence"/>
        <group id="11" type="span" parent="10" relname="span"/>
        <group id="12" type="span" parent="5" relname="background"/>
        <group id="13" type="span" parent="12" relname="span"/>
        <group id="14" type="span" parent="11" relname="span"/>
        <group id="15" type="span" parent="11" relname="antithesis"/>
    </body>
